1	Upload clear food photo	Upload a clear photo of a plate with chicken, rice, and broccoli	App identifies the foods and estimates calories, carbs, fat, protein, etc.
2	Upload blurry photo	Upload a blurry picture of food	App should indicate low confidence, request a clearer photo, or avoid presenting uncertain results as exact
3	Multiple foods on plate	Upload a plate containing several different foods	App identifies individual food items and provides nutrition estimates for each and the total
4	Single food item	Upload a photo of one apple	App identifies the apple and displays estimated nutritional information
5	Non-food photo	Upload a photo of a shoe	App should indicate that no food was detected rather than generating nutrition information
6	Empty plate	Upload a photo of an empty plate	App should recognize that there is no measurable food and not assign calories
7	Full meal consumed	Mark the entire meal as eaten	Consumed calories/nutrients should equal the original estimated totals
8	Half meal consumed	Start with a 600-calorie meal and indicate that approximately 50% was eaten	Consumed calories should update to approximately 300; carbs, fat, protein, etc. should also adjust proportionally
9	Small portion consumed	Indicate that approximately 25% of the meal was eaten	Consumed nutrition values should update to approximately 25% of the original estimates
10	Nothing consumed	Indicate that none of the meal was eaten	Consumed calories, carbs, fat, protein, etc. should be 0
11	Different foods eaten differently	Eat all the chicken, half the rice, and none of the broccoli	Nutrition totals should be recalculated based on the amount consumed of each individual food
12	Before/after photos	Upload the original meal photo, eat some food, then upload another photo	App estimates the remaining portions and calculates approximately how much was consumed
13	Food removed but not eaten	Remove food from the plate before taking the second photo	App should not automatically claim removed food was consumed unless that is an explicit assumption or the user confirms it
14	Add food after first photo	Upload initial plate, then add another food item	App should recognize that the second image contains additional food rather than treating the difference as consumption
15	Similar-looking foods	Upload mashed potatoes vs. cauliflower mash	App should provide an identification/confidence mechanism because visually similar foods can have substantially different nutrition
16	Hidden ingredients	Upload something like a cheeseburger with sauces/toppings partly hidden	App should communicate that nutrition is an estimate when ingredients cannot be determined visually
17	Portion-size uncertainty	Photograph identical food from different distances/angles	Estimates should remain reasonably consistent or warn when portion size cannot reliably be determined
18	Very large meal	Upload a plate containing an unusually large portion	App should calculate the larger serving rather than defaulting to a standard serving size
19	Invalid file	Upload a PDF/text file instead of an image	App rejects the file with an understandable error message
20	Unsupported/corrupted image	Upload a corrupted or unsupported image	App handles the error without crashing and tells the user what went wrong
